---
// Bring your own Agents: Banda reaches the Harnesses the Person already
// has, keeps what matters as text, and is open source.
import DeskSection from "./DeskSection.astro"
import Icon from "./Icon.astro"
---

<DeskSection
  id="own"
  num="06"
  label="House rules"
  quiet="Bring your own"
  loud="Agents."
>
  <p slot="say">
    Banda does not replace the Agents you already have. It gives them a place to
    work together, with you in charge.
  </p>
  <div class="glass">
    <div class="tiles">
      <div class="tile">
        <div class="vis">
          <div class="row">
            <Icon name="term" size={15} />
            Claude Code<span>in a Thread</span>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <Icon name="term" size={15} />
            Codex<span>in a Thread</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3>An adapter, not a Harness.</h3>
        <p>
          Claude Code and Codex are the Harnesses you already have. Banda shows
          their Agents, joins them and obeys them. It is not a model, and it
          does not replace one.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <div class="vis top">
          <div class="files">
            <span>plan.md</span>
            <span>report.html</span>
            <span>sidebar.json</span>
          </div>
          <div class="json">
            <span class="k">{"{"}</span>
            <span class="s">"sidebar"</span>: <span class="k">{"{"}</span>
            <br />
            &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="s">"oldestFirst"</span>:{" "}
            <span class="v">true</span>,<br />
            &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="s">"showLater"</span>:{" "}
            <span class="v">false</span>
            <br />
            <span class="k">{"}}"}</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3>Text is the common language.</h3>
        <p>
          You and an Agent talk in markdown. What is kept is md, html and json:
          files a Person and an Agent can both read, with or without Banda.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <div class="vis">
          <div class="row">
            <Icon name="github" size={15} />
            0x1oceanlabs/banda<span>GitHub</span>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <Icon name="file" size={15} />
            LICENSE<span>Apache-2.0</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3>Open source, all of it.</h3>
        <p>
          Apache-2.0, on GitHub. Read it, run it on your own machines, change
          it. An Agent can write a new App for it in a Thread.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</DeskSection>

<style>
  .tiles {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--gap-outer);
  }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .tiles {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
  .vis {
    height: 168px;
    margin: -8px -8px 20px;
    border-radius: var(--card-radius);
    background: var(--block);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--border);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .vis.top {
    justify-content: flex-start;
  }
  .row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    height: 36px;
    padding: 0 12px;
    border-radius: var(--control-radius);
    background: var(--raised);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .row span {
    margin-left: auto;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }
  .files {
    display: flex;
    gap: 6px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .files span {
    font: 12.5px/20px var(--font-family-mono);
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: var(--small-radius);
    background: var(--raised);
  }
  .json {
    font: 12.5px/20px var(--font-family-mono);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }
  .json .k {
    color: var(--foreground);
  }
  .json .s {
    color: var(--sign-teal);
  }
  .json .v {
    color: var(--sign-sand);
  }
</style>
